description: Enforce backend module folder conventions
alwaysApply: true
---

# Backend Module Structure

For any new module `<module>` (example: `ppt`, `property`, `trends`):

- API routes: `backend/app/api/routes/<module>/`
  - route code lives in files inside this folder (example: `ppt_exports.py`, `properties.py`)
  - do NOT create duplicate route modules at `backend/app/api/routes/<module>_*.py` (outside the `<module>/` folder)
- Router wiring: update `backend/app/main.py` to include:
  - `from app.api.routes.<module> import <module_file>`
  - `app.include_router(<module_file>.router, prefix=settings.API_V1_STR)`
- Models: `backend/app/models/<module>/` (SQLAlchemy models)
- Schemas: `backend/app/schemas/<module>/` (Pydantic request/response)
- Services: `backend/app/services/<module>/` for non-trivial business logic / external calls used by routes
  - if the module has no special logic yet, keep it in routes for now, but move it into `services/<module>/` when it grows
- Shared helpers: `backend/app/utils/` only for cross-cutting utilities used by multiple modules

# Single Source of Truth

Never keep two copies of the same “routes entrypoint” (like both `routes/ppt_exports.py` and `routes/ppt/ppt_exports.py`).
